    "# Python de bolsillo\n",
    "\n",
    "[← Anterior](02-lab-primer-notebook.ipynb) · [Siguiente →](../M01-fundamentos-entorno/01-teoria.ipynb)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hoja de recordatorio. **No es un curso de Python.** Es lo mínimo que vas a leer y escribir en los labs de PySpark.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ejecuta las celdas **aquí**. Si ya te suena, recorre en diagonal. Si no, quédate hasta `None` y los `import`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Pandas y Spark se ven en M01. Aquí no hay DataFrames.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ejecuta las celdas **aquí**, en este mismo fichero. No lo copies a otro sitio.\n",
    "\n",
    "Kernel: **Python (NovaShop)**.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Variables y tipos simples\n",
    "\n",
    "Un nombre guarda un valor. No declaras el tipo: Python lo ve en lo que asignas.\n",
    "\n",
    "Al ejecutar: `str`, `int`, `float`, `bool`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "39746884",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "O90001 <class 'str'>\n",
      "3 <class 'int'>\n",
      "19.9 <class 'float'>\n",
      "True <class 'bool'>\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# = asigna. == compara (más abajo).\n",
    "pedido = \"O90001\"       # str  — texto\n",
    "unidades = 3            # int  — entero\n",
    "precio = 19.90          # float — decimal\n",
    "cobrado = True          # bool — True / False (mayúscula)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(pedido, type(pedido))\n",
    "print(unidades, type(unidades))\n",
    "print(precio, type(precio))\n",
    "print(cobrado, type(cobrado))\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "f5edcbe4"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tipos compuestos\n",
    "\n",
    "Un compuesto **agrupa** varios valores. El tipo del objeto entero es `list`, `tuple`, `dict` o `set`; lo de dentro puede ser de otro tipo (una lista de `str`, un dict de `str` → `float`).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Tipo | Se escribe | Qué es | ¿Se puede cambiar? |\n",
    "|------|------------|--------|---------------------|\n",
    "| `list` | `[a, b, c]` | Secuencia ordenada | Sí (`append`, `lista[0] = …`) |\n",
    "| `tuple` | `(a, b)` o `a, b` | Secuencia ordenada, fija | No (inmutable) |\n",
    "| `dict` | `{\"k\": v}` | Clave → valor | Sí |\n",
    "| `set` | `{a, b}` | Conjunto **sin duplicados** y sin orden | Sí |\n",
    "\n",
    "Al ejecutar, `type(...)` debe decir exactamente esos cuatro nombres. Fíjate: `{1, 2}` es un `set`; `{\"a\": 1}` es un `dict` (lleva `:`).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "0e92cfb3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "list  <class 'list'> ['paid', 'cancelled', 'pending']\n",
      "tuple <class 'tuple'> ('WEB', 'app')\n",
      "dict  <class 'dict'> {'order_id': 'O1', 'amount': 10.0}\n",
      "set   <class 'set'> {'store', 'web', 'app'}\n",
      "primer estado: paid\n",
      "amount: 10.0\n",
      "cuántos estados: 3\n",
      "app está en la tupla? True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "estados = [\"paid\", \"cancelled\", \"pending\"]          # list\n",
    "punto = (\"WEB\", \"app\")                                # tuple\n",
    "pedido = {\"order_id\": \"O1\", \"amount\": 10.0}           # dict\n",
    "canales = {\"web\", \"app\", \"store\", \"web\"}              # set (el \"web\" repetido se pierde)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"list \", type(estados), estados)\n",
    "print(\"tuple\", type(punto), punto)\n",
    "print(\"dict \", type(pedido), pedido)\n",
    "print(\"set  \", type(canales), canales)  # un solo \"web\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"primer estado:\", estados[0])\n",
    "print(\"amount:\", pedido[\"amount\"])\n",
    "print(\"cuántos estados:\", len(estados))\n",
    "print(\"app está en la tupla?\", \"app\" in punto)\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "fc5f8e81"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## `print`, comentarios, f-strings\n",
    "\n",
    "`print` escribe debajo de la celda. `#` es un comentario (Python no lo ejecuta).\n",
    "\n",
    "Un f-string mete valores dentro del texto: `f\"...{nombre}...\"`. Lo usarás para mensajes, no para armar SQL a mano.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "77f675c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "pedido O1\n",
      "el pedido O1 facturó 49.9\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "order_id = \"O1\"\n",
    "gmv = 49.9\n",
    "# Esto no corre: es una nota para ti\n",
    "print(\"pedido\", order_id)\n",
    "print(f\"el pedido {order_id} facturó {gmv}\")\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "a83dfab4"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## `None` (no hay valor)\n",
    "\n",
    "En Spark verás nulos. En Python el “no hay nada” se llama `None`. Se compara con `is None`, no con `== None` (aunque a veces funcione).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "d96b17c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "True\n",
      "False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "pais = None\n",
    "print(pais is None)\n",
    "print(pais == \"\")  # False: vacío y None no son lo mismo\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "17ac9bd9"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Comparar y decidir (`if`)\n",
    "\n",
    "`==` `!=` `<` `>` `<=` `>=`. Varias condiciones: `and`, `or`, `not`.\n",
    "\n",
    "La indentación (espacios a la izquierda) **es** el bloque. Sin ella, Python falla.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "f5dd74cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "cobrado, pero el descuento está sucio\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "status = \"paid\"\n",
    "discount = 1.5\n",
    "\n",
    "if status == \"paid\" and discount > 1:\n",
    "    print(\"cobrado, pero el descuento está sucio\")\n",
    "elif status == \"cancelled\":\n",
    "    print(\"no entra en el GMV cobrable\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"otro estado:\", status)\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "67c28497"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Listas (usarlas)\n",
    "\n",
    "Índice desde **0**. `append` añade al final. En Spark casi no recorres filas con `for`; sí montas listas cortas de `Row(...)`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "7af5858d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "primero: paid\n",
      "último: pending\n",
      "trozo [0:2]: ['paid', 'cancelled']\n",
      "estado: paid\n",
      "estado: cancelled\n",
      "estado: pending\n",
      "estado: refunded\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "estados = [\"paid\", \"cancelled\", \"pending\"]\n",
    "print(\"primero:\", estados[0])\n",
    "print(\"último:\", estados[-1])\n",
    "print(\"trozo [0:2]:\", estados[0:2])  # paid, cancelled (sin el 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "estados.append(\"refunded\")\n",
    "for s in estados:\n",
    "    print(\"estado:\", s)\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "ab4499a0"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tuplas\n",
    "\n",
    "Como una lista, pero **no** le puedes hacer `append` ni `punto[0] = \"x\"`. Aparecen al devolver dos valores (`a, b = …`) y en APIs (`isin((\"web\", \"app\"))` en Spark es “¿está en esta tupla?”).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "5055ba58",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WEB 2\n",
      "WEB app\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "punto = (\"WEB\", \"app\")\n",
    "print(punto[0], len(punto))\n",
    "a, b = punto  # desempaquetar\n",
    "print(a, b)\n",
    "# punto.append(\"store\")  # AttributeError si lo descomentas\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "7ed87db2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Diccionarios (usarlos)\n",
    "\n",
    "Clave → valor. En Pandas una fila parece un dict. En Spark, `Row(campo=valor)` es la misma idea.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "3c9c1898",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "O1\n",
      "['order_id', 'status', 'amount']\n",
      "order_id = O1\n",
      "status = paid\n",
      "amount = 10.0\n",
      "channel = web\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "pedido = {\"order_id\": \"O1\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"amount\": 10.0}\n",
    "print(pedido[\"order_id\"])\n",
    "print(list(pedido.keys()))\n",
    "pedido[\"channel\"] = \"web\"  # alta o pisa\n",
    "\n",
    "for clave, valor in pedido.items():\n",
    "    print(clave, \"=\", valor)\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "3182e397"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sets\n",
    "\n",
    "Útiles para “valores únicos” y para `in` rápido. No hay `canales[0]`: no hay posición.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "c4179ab0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'store', 'web', 'app'}\n",
      "False\n",
      "{'web'}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "canales = {\"web\", \"app\", \"store\", \"web\"}\n",
    "print(canales)\n",
    "canales.add(\"other\")\n",
    "print(\"marketplace\" in canales)  # False\n",
    "print(canales & {\"web\", \"marketplace\"})  # intersección: {'web'}\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "5d48caa4"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Texto: lo que más ensucia un CSV\n",
    "\n",
    "Mayúsculas, espacios, vacío. En los labs verás `lower`, `trim` *en Spark*; aquí es el equivalente Python para que sepas qué significa.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "30241abe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WEB\n",
      "web\n",
      "True\n",
      "True False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "canal = \"  WEB \"\n",
    "print(canal.strip())          # quita espacios de los bordes\n",
    "print(canal.strip().lower())  # web\n",
    "print(\"\".strip() == \"\")       # texto vacío\n",
    "print(bool(\"WEB\"), bool(\"\"))  # True, False\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "ac38461f"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Funciones\n",
    "\n",
    "`def` nombra un trozo reutilizable. En el curso casi todo será API de Spark (`filter`, `count`). Una función tuya aparece poco; sí verás `from x import y`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "24e3d80d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "True\n",
      "False\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def es_cobrable(status):\n",
    "    return status == \"paid\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(es_cobrable(\"paid\"))\n",
    "print(es_cobrable(\"pending\"))\n"
   ]
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "25758154"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
